backend deployment with github autoupdate 
First GitHub lo backend code push cheyadaniki mee project folder open chesi Git Bash lo `git init` run cheyali, tarvatha `git remote -v` tho repository unda leda check cheyali.
Repository lekapothe `git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repo.git` tho add cheyali. 
Next `git add .` tho files add chesi, `git commit -m "Updated my code"` ani commit chesi, `git push -u origin main` tho code ni GitHub ki push cheyali.

Tarvatha AWS lo EC2 instance create chesaka, aa instance ki connect avvadaniki `ssh -i "your-key.pem" ubuntu@your-ec2-public-ip` command use cheyali.
Connect ayyaka instance lo `sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y` run chesi system update cheyali.
Tarvatha `sudo apt install git -y` tho Git install chesi, `sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk -y` tho Java install cheyali (Spring Boot ki required). 
React frontend use chesthe `sudo apt install nodejs npm -y` install cheyali.

Next step lo GitHub repo ni EC2 lo clone cheyali using `git clone https://github.com/username/repo.git` and `cd repo` command tho project folder lo ki vellali.
Appudu Maven project ayithe `mvn clean install` run chesi build cheyali. Build ayyaka application run cheyadaniki `java -jar target/your-app-name.jar` use cheyali. 
App run ayyaka browser lo `http://<EC2-IP>:8080` tho access cheyachu. App ni stop cheyadaniki Ctrl + C use cheyali, lekapothe background lo run cheyadaniki `nohup java -jar target/*.jar > app.log 2>&1 &` command use cheyali. 
Logs chudataniki `tail -f app.log` use cheyachu.

Application proper ga run avvadaniki `application.properties` lo `server.port=8080` and `server.address=0.0.0.0` set cheyali.
AWS Security Group lo 22, 8080, 9000 ports open cheyali. Auto deploy kosam EC2 lo `deploy.sh` file create chesi,
andulo repo folder ki navigate ayi `git pull origin main`, `mvn clean install`, old process stop chesi, malli `nohup java -jar target/*.jar > app.log 2>&1 &` run cheyali.
Tarvatha `chmod +x deploy.sh` tho executable ga marchali.

Webhook setup kosam `sudo apt install webhook -y` install chesi, `hooks.json` file create chesi deploy command map cheyali.
Webhook server ni `webhook -hooks hooks.json -port 9000` tho run cheyali. 
GitHub lo repo → Settings → Webhooks lo payload URL ga `http://<EC2-IP>:9000/hooks/deploy-backend` add chesi, content type `application/json` set chesi “Just push events” select cheyali. 
Ippudu eppudu GitHub lo code push chesina, webhook trigger ayi automatic ga EC2 lo code pull ayi build ayi application restart avutundi 👍

frontend deployment with github autoupdated
1. EC2 ki connect avvali
   ssh -i "your-key.pem" ubuntu@your-ec2-ip

2. Required packages install cheyali
   sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
   sudo apt install nginx git nodejs npm -y

3. Nginx start cheyali
   sudo systemctl start nginx
   sudo systemctl enable nginx

4. Rendu frontend apps kosam folders create cheyali
   sudo mkdir -p /var/www/app1
   sudo mkdir -p /var/www/app2

5. GitHub nundi projects clone cheyali
   cd /home/ubuntu
   git clone [https://github.com/username/app1.git](https://github.com/username/app1.git)
   git clone [https://github.com/username/app2.git](https://github.com/username/app2.git)

6. App1 build cheyali
   cd app1
   npm install
   npm run build
   sudo cp -r build/* /var/www/app1/

7. App2 build cheyali
   cd ../app2
   npm install
   npm run build
   sudo cp -r build/* /var/www/app2/

8. App1 kosam nginx config create cheyali
   sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/app1

server {
listen 80;
server_name app1.evyaa.com;

```
root /var/www/app1;  
index index.html;  

location / {  
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;  
}  
```

}

9. App2 kosam nginx config create cheyali
   sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/app2

server {
listen 80;
server_name app2.evyaa.com;

```
root /var/www/app2;  
index index.html;  

location / {  
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;  
}  
```

}

10. Configs enable cheyali
    sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/app1 /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
    sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/app2 /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
    sudo rm /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default
    sudo nginx -t
    sudo systemctl restart nginx

11. DNS lo records add cheyali
    app1 → EC2 IP
    app2 → EC2 IP

12. SSL install cheyali
    sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx -y
    sudo certbot --nginx -d app1.evyaa.com -d app2.evyaa.com

13. App1 deploy script create cheyali
    nano /home/ubuntu/app1/deploy.sh

#!/bin/bash
cd /home/ubuntu/app1
git pull origin main
npm install
npm run build
sudo cp -r build/* /var/www/app1/

chmod +x /home/ubuntu/app1/deploy.sh

14. App2 deploy script create cheyali
    nano /home/ubuntu/app2/deploy.sh

#!/bin/bash
cd /home/ubuntu/app2
git pull origin main
npm install
npm run build
sudo cp -r build/* /var/www/app2/

chmod +x /home/ubuntu/app2/deploy.sh

15. Webhook install cheyali
    sudo apt install webhook -y

16. hooks.json create cheyali
    nano /home/ubuntu/hooks.json

[
{
"id": "deploy-app1",
"execute-command": "/home/ubuntu/app1/deploy.sh"
},
{
"id": "deploy-app2",
"execute-command": "/home/ubuntu/app2/deploy.sh"
}
]

17. Webhook run cheyali
    nohup webhook -hooks /home/ubuntu/hooks.json -port 9000 > webhook.log 2>&1 &

18. AWS security group lo port 9000 open cheyali

19. GitHub webhook add cheyali
    App1 → [http://EC2-IP:9000/hooks/deploy-app1](http://EC2-IP:9000/hooks/deploy-app1)
    App2 → [http://EC2-IP:9000/hooks/deploy-app2](http://EC2-IP:9000/hooks/deploy-app2)
    method POST
    trigger push events

20. Test cheyali
    git add .
    git commit -m "update"
    git push origin main

21. Flow
    GitHub push → webhook trigger → EC2 git pull → build → nginx serve updated app 👍

